{"Title":"An Act relative to employment of attorneys by county retirement boards","BillNumber":"H2446","DocketNumber":"HD4036","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"D_B1","Name":"David Biele","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/D_B1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T10:35:11.983"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"D_B1","Name":"David Biele","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/D_B1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T10:35:11.9833333"},{"Id":"NMB1","Name":"Natalie M. Blais","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/NMB1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-15T14:48:47.9633333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2446/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Biele of Boston, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2446) of David Biele and Natalie M. Blais relative to the employment of attorneys by county retirement boards.  Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tNotwithstanding the provisions of any general or special law to the contrary, Chapter 32 of the Massachusetts General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is amended in Section 20(3)(e) by striking, the following:\r\n\t\"but, such attorney shall not be a member in service of the system or a member of the retirement board.\"\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}